# L §7.2 (round 6): "round(x, 1, mode) of a dimensionless num is an int, so premium * round(months / 12, 1, up) is
# money × int, money".  mons = 14, twelve = 12, premium = 100.00 PLN: 14/12 rounded up to whole units is 2, an int;
# money × int is money (L §3.2): 200.00 PLN, assigned to a money def without round.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input mons: int
input twelve: int
input premium: money PLN
def yrs: int = round(mons / twelve, 1, up) at reader
def cost: money PLN = premium * round(mons / twelve, 1, up) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  mons = 14
  twelve = 12
  premium = 100.00 PLN

ask a: yrs, cost law 2026-06-30
=== expect
a: (2, 200.00 PLN)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
